  Quote of the Week:

  Pope Julius II, in reply to Michelangelo, who had asked which of his 
artistic tools the Pope would like to try (1506):
  "Nay, give me a sword, for I am no scholar."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  With the coming of the spring season, Agraim set out to quench his thirst 
for glory.  He prepared his armies to defend Dongola and the surrounding 
provinces.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Agraim for this year.



  Here is the financial report for Agraim's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0 
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Agraim was left with 0 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Jolin
To: Agraim

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter melted into fragrant spring.  I prepared my armies to defend 
Chad and the surrounding provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Jolin


